# OpenClaw — Model Forge

## What the Forge Is

The Model Forge is the platform's AI training and deployment pipeline. It allows tenants to:
1. Create workspaces (scoped to a domain/vertical)
2. Upload and version datasets
3. Configure and submit training jobs
4. Register trained models with versioning
5. Approve model versions (human-in-loop gate)
6. Deploy approved models to live endpoints
7. Monitor eval metrics and usage events

## API Routes (all under `/api/forge/`)

```
GET    /forge/workspaces                              → List user's workspaces
POST   /forge/workspaces                              → Create workspace (auto-provisions tenant)
GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid                         → Get workspace

GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/datasets                → List datasets
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/datasets                → Create dataset
GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/datasets/:did           → Get dataset + documents
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/datasets/:did/documents → Add document
DELETE /forge/workspaces/:wid/datasets/:did/documents/:docId → Remove document
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/datasets/:did/version   → Snapshot dataset version

GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs                    → List training jobs
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs                    → Create job (status: draft)
GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid               → Get job + Kairos status
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid/submit        → Validate + queue job
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid/dispatch      → Dispatch to Kairos (status: running)
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid/cancel        → Cancel job
GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid/events        → SSE stream from Kairos
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid/deploy        → Deploy completed job
GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/jobs/:jid/eval          → Get eval runs + metrics

GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/policies                → Get governance policy
PUT    /forge/workspaces/:wid/policies                → Update policy

GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/registry                → List model registrations + versions
POST   /forge/workspaces/:wid/registry/:rid/versions/:vid/approve → Approve model version
GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/registry/:rid/deployment → Get active deployment + endpoint URL

GET    /forge/workspaces/:wid/deployments             → List deployments
```

## Training Job State Machine

```
draft → queued → running → completed → deployed
                         ↘ failed
```

- `draft`: Job created, not yet submitted
- `queued`: Passed validation (dataset ready, model allowed, concurrency OK)
- `running`: Dispatched to Kairos, `kairos_run_id` set
- `completed`: Kairos finished successfully
- `failed`: Validation failed or Kairos error
- `deployed`: Model version approved + deployment created

## Training Modes

| Mode | Description |
|---|---|
| `prompt_tuning` | Prompt engineering + few-shot examples |
| `rag_adaptation` | FAISS retrieval augmentation (primary mode for legal vertical) |
| `fine_tuning` | Full model fine-tuning (requires larger compute) |

## Governance Policy (per tenant)

Stored in `model_policies` table. Enforced at job submit time:

| Field | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `allowed_base_models` | `[]` (all allowed) | Allowlist of base model IDs |
| `max_dataset_bytes` | 100 MB | Max dataset size |
| `max_concurrent_jobs` | 2 | Max running+queued jobs |
| `deployment_requires_approval` | `true` | Human approval gate before deploy |
| `budget_limit_usd` | null | Spend cap |

## Model Approval Gate

Before a model version can be deployed:
1. Job must be in `completed` status
2. Model version must be in `candidate` status
3. Only the tenant owner (matching `userId`) can approve
4. Approval creates a record in `model_approvals` table
5. Version status moves to `approved`
6. Then `POST /jobs/:jid/deploy` creates the deployment

## Onboarding Provision

`POST /api/onboarding/provision` — called on first Forge visit for a new user.

Seeds the starter workspace with:
- Workspace: "Legal AI Operating Layer" (domain: legal)
- Dataset: CUAD Legal Clause Dataset v2 (50 examples, status: ready)
- Training job: Legal Clause Extractor v1 (mode: rag_adaptation, status: completed)
- Model registration + approved version (eval_accuracy: 1.0)
- Active deployment + endpoint: `/v1/legal/extract-clause`
- Governance policy: 3 allowed models, 3 concurrent jobs, approval required

Idempotent — safe to call multiple times.

## DB Schema (Forge tables)

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `model_workspaces` | Workspace per tenant (id, tenant_id, name, domain) |
| `model_datasets` | Dataset per workspace (source_type, sensitivity, status, document_count) |
| `dataset_versions` | Immutable snapshots of datasets |
| `dataset_documents` | Individual files/URLs in a dataset |
| `training_jobs` | Job config + state (mode, base_model, hyperparams, kairos_run_id) |
| `training_job_artifacts` | Output artifacts from completed jobs |
| `evaluation_runs` | Eval run records per job |
| `evaluation_metrics` | Per-metric results (accuracy, f1, etc.) |
| `model_registrations` | Named model registry entry per workspace |
| `model_versions` | Versioned model artifacts (status: candidate → approved) |
| `model_deployments` | Active deployments (status: pending → active) |
| `deployment_endpoints` | Callable endpoint paths per deployment |
| `model_usage_events` | Audit log of training_started, deployed, etc. |
| `model_policies` | Governance policy per tenant |
| `model_approvals` | Human approval records |

## Workspace Middleware

`requireWorkspaceMember` middleware (in `src/middleware/requireWorkspaceMember.ts`):
- Resolves `:wid` to a `model_workspaces` row
- Verifies the workspace belongs to the authenticated user's tenant
- Attaches `req.resolvedWorkspace` and `req.resolvedTenantId` to the request
- Returns 404 if workspace not found, 403 if tenant mismatch
